# Every env variant, then the template back in. `.env.backup` was listed above and
# `.env.bak.232443` still slipped through, because a named exception only ever catches the
# one name somebody thought of. This repository is PUBLIC: an env file committed here is
# readable by anyone and scraped within minutes.
.env*
!.env.example

# Keys, certificates and database dumps. A private key was committed to this repo in its
# first commit and sat in a public repository until it was found.
